diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6453d912..aa1c589d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -97,6 +97,85 @@ ninja
 
 The output DOL is written to `build/GGTE01/main.dol`, or to the folder for the version you built.
 
-Mods of the Japanese Wii release (R24J01) live in [chibirobo-wii-mod](https://github.com/LabDennis/chibirobo-wii-mod).
+### Wii mods
+
+Two options build a mod of your Japanese Wii disc, alone or together:
+
+- `--gcncon`: GameCube controller support. On the first screen, the first A
+  press picks the controls: A on a GameCube controller in port 1 plays with the
+  GameCube controller alone, and the game stops asking for the Wii Remote; A on
+  the Wii Remote plays as the Wii release does, pointer, motion and speaker
+  included. The game already maps the GameCube buttons; the release only left
+  them switched off.
+- `--langpack <locale>`: the game's text in another language (see below).
+
+```sh
+python3 configure.py --version R24J01 --gcncon --langpack en-US
+ninja
+```
+
+Open `build/wii-en-US-gcncon/game.json` in Dolphin (the folder is named after the
+options: `wii-gcncon`, `wii-en-US`, …). Dolphin applies the mod to your original
+disc image; on a Wii, Riivolution does the same with the folder's
+`riivolution.xml` and `main.dol`.
+
+Add `--iso` to also get a disc image with the mod, for example
+`build/wii-en-US-gcncon/wii-en-US-gcncon.iso`. This needs
+[Wiimms ISO Tools](https://wit.wiimm.de) (`wit`, GPL-2.0) on your PATH, in
+`~/.local/opt/wit/bin/wit`, or passed with `--wit`. The build extracts your disc
+once, puts the mod's `main.dol` and files into a copy, and has `wit` write and
+encrypt the image. Ticket and TMD are fake-signed: Dolphin plays it as is; a Wii
+needs a USB loader with patched IOS.
+
+With `--iso`, `--fanpatch <folder>` also puts a translation patch made for the
+retail disc into the image: the folder Riivolution loads, with the patch's
+`main.dol` and its file folders. Like Riivolution, its files replace the disc's
+files of the same name, whatever the case of their names. Its changes to
+`main.dol` are found by their surrounding data and copied to the same data in
+the mod's `main.dol`; this suits a patch that only rewrites text, as the
+V0101 English patch does. The image is then named `…-fanpatch.iso`. The build
+stops if a change has no unique place in the mod.
+
+Use `--langpack global` for Japanese, English, German, French, Spanish and
+Italian in one build. The game reads the Wii system language at startup and uses
+English for other language settings. Japanese uses the original resources.
+To lock the language, choose `en-US`, `en-GB`, `de-DE`, `fr-FR`, `es-ES` or
+`it-IT`. GameCube controller support works with either selection.
+
+```sh
+python3 configure.py --version R24J01 --langpack global
+ninja
+python3 configure.py --version R24J01 --langpack global --gcncon --iso
+ninja
+```
+
+Global builds require `tools/wii_lang_data.py` and the disc images in
+`orig/R24J01`, `orig/GGTE01` and `orig/GGTP01`. Ninja generates the assets in
+`build/wii-lang/files/lang/` once for both controller configurations. It installs
+the language directories in `build/wii-global/files/lang/` or
+`build/wii-global-gcncon/files/lang/`. These generated directories are replaced
+when the inputs change. Riivolution and the optional ISO use the same files.
+The disc images are named `wii-global.iso` and `wii-global-gcncon.iso` in their
+respective output folders. Available translations depend on the disc data.
+The game falls back to the original file when a language override is missing.
+
+Runtime interface and PC text use the GameCube string tables resident in the
+Wii executable. Wii-specific translations and the title and save banner lines
+are in `mods/wii-localization/`.
+These mods share the Japanese title's save files. Use a separate Dolphin user
+directory to keep a development save. Retail progress is measured against `R24J01`.
+
+To import actor, costume and stage names, extract the desired language's
+`globals.bin` from your GameCube disc's `qp.bin`. Pass that file and the
+original Wii file to the importer. For an English build:
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/wii_stage_names.py path/to/gc/globals.bin orig/R24J01/files/bin/globals.bin build/wii-en-US/files/bin/globals.bin
+```
+
+The importer lists skipped IDs and keeps their Japanese names. It accepts
+printable ASCII by default. Add `--fold-cp1252` to convert supported Western
+accents to ASCII. Object collisions, stage descriptions and event scripts
+come from the Wii file.
 
